Description: A toolkit for differential analysis of omics data. Implements a
    CPLM-based statistical workflow built on the Tweedie distribution. Unlike
    traditional single-omics tools, Tweedieverse is technology-agnostic and
    can be applied to both count and continuous measurements arising from
    diverse high-throughput technologies (e.g. transcript abundances from bulk
    and single-cell RNA-Seq studies in the form of UMI counts or non-UMI
    counts, microbiome taxonomic and functional profiles in the form of counts
    or relative abundances, and compound abundance levels or peak intensities
    from metabolomics and other mass spectrometry-based experiments, among
    others). The software includes multiple customization options such as the
    inclusion of random effects and multiple covariates along with several
    data exploration capabilities and visualization modules in a unified
    estimation umbrella.
Depends: R (>= 4.6.0)
